# Frontend environment. Copy to apps/web/.env for local development.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the bundle AT BUILD TIME. Two
# consequences worth internalising before deploying:
#   - Changing either value in Vercel requires a REDEPLOY, not just a restart.
#   - Never put a secret here. Anything VITE_* ships to the browser in plain
#     text; only publishable/public keys belong in this file.

# Clerk publishable key (required). Safe to expose — it is the public half.
# A pk_test_ key works in production but renders a "Development mode" banner on
# the sign-in card, so use a production Clerk instance for the real deploy.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Base URL of the worker API. No trailing slash.
# Local: http://localhost:8787   Production: https://<your-worker>.onrender.com
# Whatever you set here must also appear in the worker's WEB_ORIGIN allowlist
# from the other direction, or every tRPC call fails CORS.
VITE_WORKER_URL=http://localhost:8787
